This Document contains all information related to the new functionality around addition of a new product type named Junior Investment and Saving Account.

Current available product types under a new member 

When we add a new member under any advisor , they have the option to add any of the following product types - 

 1. GIA - Genral Investment Account
 2. TSA - Tax Saving Account
 3. Pensions Account 

 Whenever we add a new member , we can search for the member and then add any of the above product types to it. 

 We will now we able to also add Junior investment and savings account type along with above 3 types. 

 What does each product type mean - 

 1. GIA - general investment Account 
 This is a normal investment account and is taxed for all purchases and transactions

 2. TSA - tax saving Account 
 There is no tax applied upto a limit of 20k pounds . The maximum limit for this product type is thus 20k pounds for every financial year

 3. Pension Account 
 We make regular contributions to this account type for our future savings into the pension.

 4. JISA - Junior Investment and Savings Account 
 This is similar to general investments account but has a upper limit of 10k pounds and is for teaching future investors which are currently in the age group of 12-18 years. 


Below is the journey for onboarding a new member onto the platform - 

1. Open the Admin site 
2. Navigate to Admin tab 
3. Select Member Setup and then individual member setup from the dropdown 
4. Enter the member details and fill the necessary details in the next steps of the form 
5. Submit the entered member details for authorisation 
6. Logout from the current admin user session and login with a different admin account 
7. Navigate to Admin tab 
8. Select the Authorisations option and then select new member setup from the dropdown.
9. You will see a list of all the members which are newly onboarded and needs authorisation.
10. Choose your account and click on authorise next to the member name 
11. You will see all the details entered by the first Admin and you can verify it and then click on Authorise. 
12. You new member is created . You can note the member id displayed on the screen. 

Below is the journey for adding a new product type to a member - 

1. Open the member site 
2. Navigate to client Search tab 
3. Enter the member id or name in the search form and click on search 
4. You will be redirected to member summary page where you can see the current product types of the member what holdings each of them has.
3. Click on New product option 
4. You will the available product types you can add amongst GIA,TSA, Pension Account and JISA.
5. Choose the product type you want to add and click on next 
6. Enter the necessary details in the form and click on submit 
7. The new product type will added under that member 


What are the important tables in the backend and what all details do they store - 

Table name is in the following form - 

<Database>.<Schema>.<TableName>


Tables - 

1. Accounts.dbo.Users table
This Stores the details of all users on the platform, from admin users, advisors to all the members on the platform

Columns - 
clientId - type - INT - primary key 
userName - type - VARCHAR(50) - stores the unique username of each user 
userRole - type - INT - References to roleId of Accounts.dbo.UserRoles table and tells about the role of the user in the platform.
dateCreated - type - DATETIME - the date member/admin/user was created/added to platform

2. Accounts.dbo.UserRoles table
This stores the various user roles available on the platform for authorisation purpose.

Columns- 
roleId - type - INT - primary key 
roleDescription - type - VARCHAR(250) - description about the user role 

3. Accounts.dbo.Members table
This table stores the records only for the members created in the platform and not any other user type 

Columns 
memberId - type - INT - primary key 
clientId - type - INT - refrence clientId of Account.dbo.Users table 
memberName - type - VARCHAR(100) - name of the member
dob - type - DATETIME - date of birth of the member 
salary - type - INT - salary of the member 
dateAdded - type - DATETIME - date added to the platform 
phone - type - INT - contact number of the member 
email - type - VARCHAR(50) - contact email address of the member 

4. Accounts.dbo.MemberProducts table 
Stores data about the different products under each member 

Columns 
memberProductid - type - INT - primary key 
memberId - type - INT - references memberId of Account.dbo.Members table, defines the parent member under which the product is present
memberProductCode - type - VARCHAR(50) - this is member id concatenated with product type like 3764-GIA , 4432-JISA 
productType - type - VARCHAR(10) - this is the product type - JISA/GIA/TSA/Pensions
productAddedDate - type - DATETIME - date on which product was added 



